.github.com/users/rorychatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ivy-Interactive/Ivy-Framework/commits/127930b71719cc60006df16f0f504bae4d631055/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:21:44Z","email":"40919111+rorychatt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Mikael Rinne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:21:44Z","email":"40919111+rorychatt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Mikael Rinne"},"message":"Share one IVY_TLS parser and drop dead OS fallback in DesktopWindow\n\nCreate TlsPolicy.IsEnabled to parse IVY_TLS tokens (\"1\", \"true\", \"yes\", \"on\")\nshared by Server.cs and DesktopWindow.cs. Replace three copies of the literal\ntest with one helper, add InternalsVisibleTo for Ivy.Desktop, and hoist useTls\ncomputation in DesktopWindow to remove the dead OS predicate fallback at :298.\n\nAdd TlsPolicyTests covering accepted/rejected tokens, unrecognized values, and\nfallback behavior. No behavior change on any platform.\n\nPlan 00483\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b99172e2e511d312b76f5b2af3eb5f552fa23219","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ivy-Interactive/Ivy-Framework/git/trees/b99172e2e511d312b76f5b2af3eb5f552fa23219"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ivy-Interactive/Ivy-Framework/git/commits/127930b71719cc60006df16f0f504bae4d631055","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40919111?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt/gists{/gist_