/rorychatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ivy-Interactive/Ivy-Framework/commits/f70aa7b92f6440b9c5d516c3c039a902265f51a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:19:44Z","email":"40919111+rorychatt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Mikael Rinne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:19:44Z","email":"40919111+rorychatt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Mikael Rinne"},"message":"Extract bind host and scheme derivation into BindHostPolicy\n\nReplace inline environment variable reads in BuildWebApplication with a new\nBindHostPolicy class containing three types: BindEnvironment (process state),\nBindAddress (bind result), and Resolve (pure derivation logic). The whole\ndecision matrix (container, PORT, host argument, CLI command, IVY_TLS) is\nnow unit-testable without mutating process-wide environment variables.\n\nAdd BindHostPolicyTests.cs with full coverage of host resolution, scheme\nselection, URL composition, and cross-checks against CorsOriginPolicy. The\nscheme default (TLS for Windows local dev only) has end-to-end coverage for\nthe first time.\n\nRefs #00482\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1cea8b3128dece2b875a3f635b836100372f4276","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ivy-Interactive/Ivy-Framework/git/trees/1cea8b3128dece2b875a3f635b836100372f4276"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ivy-Interactive/Ivy-Framework/git/commits/f70aa7b92f6440b9c5d516c3c039a902265f51a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40919111?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rorychatt/followers","followi