:"niels@bosmainteractive.se","name":"nielsbosma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:26:54Z","email":"niels@bosmainteractive.se","name":"nielsbosma"},"message":"feat(wireframe): add eight wireframe widgets, theme fonts, and ivyml run\n\nWireframe widget family: WireframePlaceholder, WireframeScratchOut,\nWireframeRedX, WireframeArrow, WireframeCurlyBrace, WireframeShape,\nWireframeMockup and WireframeTransform, each with a C# widget, a React\nrenderer, a sample app and a widgetMap registration. WireframeNote and\nWireframeCallout were reworked to match.\n\nTheme fonts: Theme gains FontFamilyMono, FontFamilySerif and a FontFaces\nlist emitted as @font-face rules ahead of the theme variables, so a theme\ncan name a web font without the host app shipping a stylesheet. Font\nvalues are escaped because the generated <style> block is re-parsed as XML.\n\nIvyML theming: --theme takes a YAML file or a built-in theme name, and a\ntheme.yaml next to the IvyML file is picked up automatically. --no-theme\nturns both off. Ships a built-in \"wireframes\" theme.\n\nIvyML run: a new `ivyml run` command serves a file as a live application.\nStudio''s preview panel now drives that as a child process instead of\nrendering in-process, so framework changes appear in the preview after a\nrebuild rather than requiring a Studio restart.\n\nAlso: `ivyml draw` installs Chromium on first use instead of failing with\na command for the user to run by hand.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fSvSpjyUR87QernSRR7Zr","tree":{"sha":"5a398a5bc551d1f9920fe5c43035ba1cb8a29308","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ivy-Interactive/Ivy-Framework/git/trees/5a398a5bc551d1f9920fe5c43035ba1cb8a29308"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ivy-Interactive/Ivy-Framework/git/commits/8d1476c6751c5c8ded226f0bab94c3c9f905220f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuse